front:
**greet(name, greeting?, punctuation?)**

Write `greet`: `greeting` defaults to `"Hello"` and `punctuation` is optional (`"!"` when missing). `greet("Ada")` → `"Hello, Ada!"`.

```ts
function greet(name: string, greeting: string, punctuation: string): string {
  return `${greeting}, ${name}${punctuation}`;
}
```

back:
// Why: A default value also gives the parameter its type (string) and makes it optional;
// passing undefined uses the default.
// Docs: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/functions.html
function greet(name: string, greeting = "Hello", punctuation?: string): string {
  return `${greeting}, ${name}${punctuation ?? "!"}`;
}

starter_code:
function greet(name: string, greeting: string, punctuation: string): string {
  return `${greeting}, ${name}${punctuation}`;
}

type_tests:
greet("Ada");
greet("Ada", "Hi");
// @ts-expect-error: name is required
greet();
// @ts-expect-error: greeting is a string
greet("Ada", 5);

