**Overloads for parse(value)**

`parse` turns a string into a number and a number into a 2-decimal string, but callers always get `string | number`. Add overload signatures so `parse("42")` is a number and `parse(3)` a string.

```ts
function parse(value: string | number): string | number {
  return typeof value === "string" ? Number(value) : value.toFixed(2);
}
```

back:
// Why: Callers see only the overload signatures; the last signature is the
// implementation's and must be compatible with all of them.
// Docs: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/functions.html
function parse(value: string): number;
function parse(value: number): string;
function parse(value: string | number): string | number {
  return typeof value === "string" ? Number(value) : value.toFixed(2);
}

